1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:08,650
TAMA Information Display is an ambient information display for a four K OLED touch
screen, now enhanced with WebMCP.

2
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:21,650
The page registers seven tools through a thin adapter. The agent reads the real
display state instead of guessing, while the original touch interface remains
unchanged.

3
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:29,650
First, we type: Show the weather in Nara.

4
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:43,650
The WebMCP host invokes show weather. The tool reuses the existing weather controller
and router, and the visible display immediately changes to Weather.

5
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:51,650
Next, we type: Show Nara Go.

6
00:00:52,350 --> 00:01:07,650
Open web page validates the requested URL, maps it to the bundled same origin copy,
and switches the display to Web. The original and simple views remain available.

7
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:15,650
Now we type: Display a meeting from one P M.

8
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:31,650
Show information renders the title and message as safe text, with priority and
duration metadata. Agent Activity makes the action visible and undoable.

9
00:01:32,350 --> 00:01:39,650
Finally, we type: Return to the original screen.

10
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:53,650
Show ambient restores the quiet clock and the human selected ambient category. The
result comes directly from the display controller.

11
00:01:54,350 --> 00:02:08,650
This adapter is feature detected. Browsers without document dot model context skip
registration safely, and manual human changes always outrank agent actions and
automatic defaults.

12
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:17,650
TAMA Information Display. One shared screen, controlled transparently by people and
agents.
